  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "section": "narrative",
      "text": "Halifax JD151 of 78 Squadron was returning from Nuremberg on 11 August 1943 short of fuel. Waiting seventh in the landing queue at Breighton, two engines cut out and the pilot lost control. The aircraft crashed at 06.19 near Bowthorpe Hall, South Duffield. Navigator Harry Binns and air gunner Thomas Gillicker died; flight engineer William John Brown died of his injuries on 13 August. The other four crew were injured.",
      "cites": [
        "C7",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "section": "memorial_details",
      "text": "A small plaque to JD151 stands in Intake Plantation, Wressle, about two miles from where the aircraft crashed. Yorkshire Aircraft, the only source found, says this is the wrong location and suggests a mix-up at the Yorkshire Air Museum. The wood has no public right of way. The source does not say who arranged the plaque or who maintains it.",
      "cites": [
        "C8",
        "C9",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "section": "community_connection",
      "text": "Albert Pritchard, Eric Barton and Ken Reast located the correct crash site near Bowthorpe Hall.",
      "cites": [
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "custodian_status": "unknown-confirmed",
  "retractions": [
    {
      "field": "community_connection",
      "reason": "'The Yorkshire Air Museum is associated with the original plaque' is not stated by any source; Yorkshire Aircraft only suggests a museum display caused the location mix-up."
    },
    {
      "field": "memorial_details",
      "reason": "Existing text says the plaque marks DT524, not JD151. The source says the plaque commemorates JD151 but stands at the wrong site; no separate DT524 plaque is described. Replaced by a sourced paragraph."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "WRESSLE VERDICT: one plaque, not two (see wressle-halifax-dt524 notes). Yorkshire Aircraft describes one plaque, commemorating JD151, in Intake Plantation near the DT524 crash site; the real JD151 site is near Bowthorpe Hall. Our record has this the wrong way round ('marks DT524 not JD151'), so the retraction replaces it. Custodian not found. CONFLICT O'NEILL: our record has Sgt Gerald John O'Neill, service no. 550757; Yorkshire Aircraft has F/Lt Gerald John O'Neill DFM RAF 47705. Our narrative says F/Lt is unconfirmed, but this source says it. Only the one source read, so no second source to settle it; check CWGC/IBCC/Aircrew Remembered. Brown's burial: ours says Allerton Sec 16 RC Gr 517; source gives cemetery only. Aircrew Remembered (jenkinson-j) was not fetched. Barger's later life (died 2012) comes from RAFCommands forum per the source; not claimed here. Single publisher."
}